 * This is a Halide translation of the original init_array().
 *
 * In the original C code, A is declared as DATA_TYPE A[N][N] and
 * accessed as A[i][j] (row i, column j). Here we store A in a
 * Halide::Buffer<num_t, 2> with dimensions (x = column j, y = row i),
 * so A[i][j] maps to A(j, i).
